WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:05.609
Marvel Studios generally runs a pretty tight
ship when it comes to spoilers, with one big

00:00:05.609 --> 00:00:10.830
exception: Spider-Man star Tom Holland, who
has become known as a bit of a spoiler machine.

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:15.370
So it's no surprise that information has started
to come out about Spider-man's next big screen

00:00:15.370 --> 00:00:16.680
solo adventure.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:21.850
Here's a look at every Spider-Man: Far From
Home rumor and spoiler leaked so far.

00:00:21.850 --> 00:00:23.390
Spider-man: Field Trip

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:29.060
In late May of 2018, a rumor with some specific
details surfaced on Reddit, posted by a user

00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:31.070
named "A Harbinger Of Stuff."

00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:35.290
Citing only a "reliable source," it offered
a breakdown of the Homecoming sequel that

00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:40.050
included Peter Parker traveling to London
for some kind of conference, Mysterio as the

00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:45.129
main villain, Scorpion and Vulture in minor
roles, and the introduction of Alistair Smythe,

00:00:45.129 --> 00:00:47.960
a.k.a. the Spider Slayer in the Marvel comics.

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:52.699
Among other details, the user claimed there
would be an MI6 agent in the film named Jessica

00:00:52.699 --> 00:00:57.440
Drew, a name comics fans will recognize as
the secret identity of the original Spider-Woman.

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:04.520
"And this is Jessica Drew, who, as a child
while visiting her father's laboratory, was

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:06.380
bitten by a poisonous spider!"

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:11.040
Though many of these rumors are still unconfirmed,
several do line up with what we know about

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:12.040
the film.

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:15.940
One detail that has been proven wrong, though,
is the name of the movie.

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:21.250
Marvel Studios head honcho Kevin Feige explained
in an interview with io9 that the name Spider-Man:

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:25.100
Far From Home was chosen in part because of
the film's international flavor.

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:28.850
"We shoot a lot of films in London but there’s
another reason we’re shooting in London

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:32.820
which is, yes, Spidey, of course, will spend
some time in New York, but he’ll spend some

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:35.400
time in other parts of the globe."

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:37.030
Matt or Jake

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:42.420
In May 2018, reports surfaced that Jake Gyllenhaal
was set to play Spidey villain Mysterio in

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:47.742
the second Sony/Marvel Studios Spider-Man
film, though in June, Feige clarified that

00:01:47.742 --> 00:01:50.670
Gyllenhaal's involvement wasn't actually confirmed
yet.

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:55.030
Gyllenhaal was reportedly the second big actor
rumored to be in talks to play a Spidey villain.

00:01:55.030 --> 00:01:59.990
According to Meet the Movie Press, Matt Damon
was approached by Marvel, but ultimately passed.

00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:05.110
Too bad, because based on his previous experience
as a supervillain, it would have been epic.

00:02:05.110 --> 00:02:11.940
"This control activates my atomic bomb, which
can destroy the entire Earth"

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:13.380
Old friends

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:18.100
According to Variety, Michael Keaton's Vulture
isn't done with Peter Parker just yet.

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:22.400
Keaton's reportedly set to reprise his role
as the villain, who'll be working alongside

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:24.840
Mysterio in Spider-Man: Far from Home.

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:28.780
The report doesn't say how prominently Vulture
will be featured, but it's already fueled

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:33.260
speculation that the films are building toward
an introduction of the Sinister Six.

00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:36.660
Vulture isn't the only Homecoming alumnus
reported to return.

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:42.320
We're also expecting to see Marisa Tomei as
Aunt May, Zendaya as MJ, Jacob Batalon as

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:46.970
Peter Parker's best bud Ned Leeds, and director
Jon Watts behind the camera.

00:02:46.970 --> 00:02:48.970
Smoove Operator

00:02:48.970 --> 00:02:52.570
In July 2018, Deadline reported that actor
and comedian J.B.

00:02:52.570 --> 00:02:57.320
Smoove had joined Spider-Man: Far from Home's
cast in an unspecified leading role.

00:02:57.320 --> 00:03:01.260
Considering he's best known for his comic
turns in Curb Your Enthusiasm and films like

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:05.790
Hall Pass, though, chances are he's going
to bring the humor to whatever role he plays.

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:09.350
And hey, he already knows exactly what a superhero
sidekick's role is.

00:03:09.350 --> 00:03:13.200
"Little emotional service doggies that lick
your face and make you feel good about yourself

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:17.310
mmm mmm and they tinkle all over your shirt
and they're so happy to see you and makes

00:03:17.310 --> 00:03:18.280
you feel good inside"

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:20.300
Another MCU character

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:25.750
In June 2017, The Hollywood Reporter said
that another already established hero would

00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:29.540
be joining Spider-Man in Far from Home, but
it wouldn't be his MCU mentor Iron Man.

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:31.950
So who is it?

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:36.980
Well, back in 2017, director Jon Watts told
ScreenRant he'd love to see Spidey team up

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:38.020
with Black Widow.

00:03:38.020 --> 00:03:41.569
"I like to think of what he could learn from
Black Widow, but then I think he would be

00:03:41.569 --> 00:03:43.740
too nervous to even get a single word out."

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:48.280
We do know who it won't be, though, as Slashfilm
asked Fiege if Doctor Strange would be guest-starring.

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:51.890
"I could be coy about it, but no."

00:03:51.890 --> 00:03:53.480
Dates to remember

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:59.030
Far from Home's July 5th, 2019 arrival, only
two months after Avengers 4, puts it in an

00:03:59.030 --> 00:04:00.150
interesting spot.

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:04.430
Its relation to Avengers 4 suggests it'll
be much more defined by its position in the

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:06.290
MCU than its predecessor.

00:04:06.290 --> 00:04:11.651
Not only does it kick off Phase 4, but producer
Amy Pascal said in June 2017 that Far from

00:04:11.651 --> 00:04:16.609
Home opens "a few minutes" after the resolution
of Avengers 4, suggesting Pete will still

00:04:16.609 --> 00:04:19.269
be dealing with the aftermath of the battle
against Thanos.

00:04:19.269 --> 00:04:21.670
And Fiege backed that up, telling io9,

00:04:21.670 --> 00:04:26.200
"The way Civil War […] informed Homecoming,
the two Avengers films that precede [Far From

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:28.210
Home] will greatly inform [...] the next movie."

00:04:28.210 --> 00:04:31.169
A new suit?

00:04:31.169 --> 00:04:35.380
Spider-Man: Homecoming costume designer Louise
Frogley may have unintentionally dropped a

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:39.790
spoiler that Peter Parker will be taking a
new costume into battle during Spider-Man:

00:04:39.790 --> 00:04:40.790
Far From Home.

00:04:40.790 --> 00:04:44.250
Though she isn't actually working on Far from
Home, she told IndiaWest,

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:48.870
"The costumes will have very big changes because,
in the film, Spider-Man becomes more like

00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:50.340
a man and not a teenager."

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:55.220
So does she have some kind of inside information
even though she's not working on the film?

00:04:55.220 --> 00:04:56.250
Hmm.

00:04:56.250 --> 00:04:58.180
Taking control of the story

00:04:58.180 --> 00:05:02.571
When Tom Holland "leaked" the title of Spider-man:
Far From Home on his Instagram account, it

00:05:02.571 --> 00:05:05.590
seemed like yet another slip-up from Marvel's
fountain of spoilers.

00:05:05.590 --> 00:05:10.810
"What I do know is I've got the new script,
I'm super excited to read it, and...it's gonna

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:11.810
be great!

00:05:11.810 --> 00:05:13.430
So ya, Spider-Man 2, let's do this!"

00:05:13.430 --> 00:05:16.660
But Feige told Birth.Death.Movies that it
was completely intentional.

00:05:16.660 --> 00:05:20.509
"There are certain logistics of the way these
movies are made that meant that title would

00:05:20.509 --> 00:05:24.090
potentially be leaked in some way because
it was going out into the world in various

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:25.090
forms.

00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:28.030
So Mr. Holland took it upon himself to leak
it for us."

00:05:28.030 --> 00:05:31.879
You know what they say about spoilers: with
great power comes great responsibility.

